       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 25,500 mg/day of metformin is in the overdose range. There is no clinical indication for it, and it could cause life-threatening lactic acidosis in a patient with normal kidney and liver function. Entering it would put the patient at serious risk.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals.** This is a standard dose, and I can enter it right now.\n- **Enter a different dose.** Tell me the dose you want, up to the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day, for example 1,000 mg twice daily.\n- **Talk to pharmacy.** If you have a specific reason for a nonstandard dose, a pharmacist can review it and enter it through the appropriate override process.\n\nWhich would you like?"
